 ## Overview
-HashNeRF parameters configure the training loop and model architecture for the HashNeRF method, which replaces the multi-resolution hash grid of Instant-NGP with a single-resolution hashed embedding table to reduce memory overhead and simplify hyperparameter tuning [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard NeRF which uses positional encoding or fixed-resolution grids, HashNeRF uses a learnable hash map indexed by voxel coordinates, requiring specific settings for the embedding table size, loss regularization, and dataset-specific loading behaviors [S1, unofficial].
